WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:14.664
It was movie day at Kids Central.

2
00:00:14.665 --> 00:00:18.072
The kids had just watched a cartoon.

3
00:00:18.073 --> 00:00:21.749
When it was over, Miss Shelly turned on the lights.

4
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.865
"I love cartoons, especially space adventures," Jason said.

5
00:00:26.866 --> 00:00:30.934
"Miss Shelly, can we draw pictures from the movie?"

6
00:00:30.935 --> 00:00:34.991
"Jason is really good at drawing," Ethan said.

7
00:00:34.992 --> 00:00:38.941
"My mom just signed me up for art lessons," Jason said.

8
00:00:38.942 --> 00:00:41.228
"My first lesson is today."

9
00:00:41.229 --> 00:00:43.575
"Fun!" Izzie said.

10
00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.677
Jason looked unsure.

11
00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.659
"I hope the teacher doesn't tell me what to draw.

12
00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.650
I like drawing my own stuff."

13
00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:57.699
"Well, I think you'll like today's drawing activity, Jason," Miss Shelly said.

14
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.201
"We're going to make flip books.

15
00:01:00.202 --> 00:01:04.616
We'll draw cartoons and turn them into movies."

16
00:01:04.617 --> 00:01:08.131
"That's called animation!" Jason said.

17
00:01:08.132 --> 00:01:12.364
"Right!" Miss Shelly smiled and held up a small booklet.

18
00:01:12.365 --> 00:01:14.458
"This is my flip book.

19
00:01:14.459 --> 00:01:18.432
I made a movie with a dancing dot. Watch."

20
00:01:18.433 --> 00:01:21.431
Miss Shelly flipped the pages of her book.

21
00:01:21.432 --> 00:01:25.041
A dot with feet danced across the paper.

22
00:01:25.042 --> 00:01:30.461
"It looks like that dot is really moving," Izzie said.

23
00:01:30.462 --> 00:01:34.276
Miss Shelly handed out three sheets of paper to everyone.

24
00:01:34.277 --> 00:01:39.234
"Stack the sheets of paper and fold them in half," she said.

25
00:01:39.235 --> 00:01:43.880
"Cut along the fold so you get two stacks of paper.

26
00:01:43.881 --> 00:01:48.951
Next fold each stack in half lengthwise.

27
00:01:48.952 --> 00:01:53.182
Cut each fold and now you'll have—"

28
00:01:53.183 --> 00:01:56.190
"Twelve strips," Jason said.

29
00:01:56.191 --> 00:02:02.286
"Yep. Now stack the strips and fold that stack in half."

30
00:02:02.287 --> 00:02:07.754
"Now we staple the pages on the folded side, right?" Ethan asked.

31
00:02:07.755 --> 00:02:10.780
"That makes a booklet with 24 pages."

32
00:02:10.781 --> 00:02:17.981
"Right. After that, I'll show you how to start drawing," Miss Shelly said.

33
00:02:17.982 --> 00:02:22.452
"Can I make a basketball go into a hoop?" Bobby asked.

34
00:02:22.453 --> 00:02:25.492
"Great idea," Miss Shelly said.

35
00:02:25.493 --> 00:02:29.207
"I'm going to draw a boy surfing," Ethan said.

36
00:02:29.208 --> 00:02:34.367
Jason smiled. He knew what he wanted to draw.

37
00:02:34.368 --> 00:02:38.752
"Turn to the last page of your flip book," Miss Shelly said.

38
00:02:38.753 --> 00:02:44.386
"Your first drawing goes here." She pointed to the lower part of the page.

39
00:02:44.387 --> 00:02:47.072
Everyone started drawing.

40
00:02:47.073 --> 00:02:51.446
"I'm making someone jumping rope," said Nina.

41
00:02:51.447 --> 00:02:54.681
"Turn to the next page," Miss Shelly said.

42
00:02:54.682 --> 00:02:57.538
"Can you see your drawing through the paper?"

43
00:02:57.539 --> 00:02:59.533
Everyone nodded.

44
00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:04.753
"Trace that drawing—except for the part that is going to move.

45
00:03:04.754 --> 00:03:06.998
You'll draw that part again.

46
00:03:06.999 --> 00:03:11.794
But you'll draw it in a different place," Miss Shelly explained.

47
00:03:11.795 --> 00:03:14.173
"I get it," Jason said.

48
00:03:14.174 --> 00:03:16.926
"Each page shows the same picture.

49
00:03:16.927 --> 00:03:21.445
But something in the picture has moved just a little bit."

50
00:03:21.446 --> 00:03:23.722
"Yep!" Miss Shelly said.

51
00:03:23.723 --> 00:03:26.726
"Start making animations, kids!"

52
00:03:26.727 --> 00:03:34.074
Page by page, Bobby drew the basketball closer to the hoop.

53
00:03:34.075 --> 00:03:38.820
Then he flipped the pages from the back to the front.

54
00:03:38.821 --> 00:03:42.555
"Yes! The basketball flies into the hoop!"

55
00:03:42.556 --> 00:03:44.423
Izzie tried hers next.

56
00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:47.891
Her frog, Gurpy, hopped across the page.

57
00:03:47.892 --> 00:03:52.501
"Look at Ethan's movie," Nina said.

58
00:03:52.502 --> 00:03:56.402
"He made a shark appear behind the surfer!"

59
00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:58.589
Jason held up his flip book.

60
00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.579
He flipped through the pages.

61
00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:02.605
A spaceship appeared.

62
00:04:02.606 --> 00:04:07.756
It sucked a dog into the ship and flew away.

63
00:04:07.757 --> 00:04:10.951
"That's the best one!" Bobby cried.

64
00:04:10.952 --> 00:04:15.234
"I want to make more movies." Jason grinned.

65
00:04:15.235 --> 00:04:22.246
"Hey! Maybe my new drawing teacher can give me some tips today."
